    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: return `membershipTier: 'SILVER'` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `'BRONZE'`.\n\nI made two changes, following the existing conventions for computed owner fields:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`). This regenerates the `OwnerDto` with the new field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipTier` and a small `formatMembershipTier(Owner)` default method that encapsulates the tier logic, mirroring the existing `formatMembershipNumber` / `formatDisplayName` / `formatInitials` helpers. It returns `SILVER` only when the owner has no namesakes (`namesakeCount == 0`) and a non-blank email, otherwise `BRONZE` (null-safe throughout).\n\nI put the logic in the mapper because that's exactly where the other derived DTO fields already live \u2014 each in its own single-responsibility helper \u2014 so nothing became a catch-all.\n\nTest results:\n- The two new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass.\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
